Replace teal with indigo-violet on navy-slate surfaces

User preferred the grey-box look of safwanhakim.com but wanted a purple
accent, having rejected both the original violet and the teal.

Accent choice:
- Took the neutral structure from safwanhakim.com's actual stylesheet:
  #0a0e17 page, #101828 card, #1a2436 raised surface. His accent is gold
  (#d4af37), so the purple is ours; what we borrowed is the navy-slate
  neutrality that makes boxes read as panels rather than holes.
- Accent is #8b7cf6, an indigo-leaning violet rather than flat #8b5cf6.
  Picked by measuring candidates against --bg-secondary: 5.33:1, versus
  4.19:1 for the original. This keeps the accent legible on cards, not just
  on the page background, which was the weakest part of the first purple.
- Swapped all 113 hardcoded teal rgba values back to the new accent trio,
  plus the navy-tinted navbar and modal overlays.

Grey-box surfaces:
- Made .card translucent (rgb(26 36 54 / 0.62) with backdrop blur), the way
  Safwan's --surface is rgba(26,36,54,.62). A translucent slate lets the
  hero gradient read through stacked cards, which is what produces the
  layered grey-panel feel rather than flat opaque rectangles.
- Seven page-level components set their own opaque --bg-secondary and would
  have overridden that, so they were converted to match.
- Card hover border now uses color-mix so it lands at 45% accent instead of
  the full accent, which was very hot on the lighter base.

Also removed a stray cm.tmp that an earlier commit picked up, and updated
theme-color in index.html and manifest.json to the new base.

Note: the repo's build/ directory is currently locked by a VS Code process,
so verification was done against a BUILD_PATH build in scratch. Same source,
clean compile, all five routes serve 200. The local build folder should
regenerate normally once the editor releases it.

Verified: compiled CSS contains #8b7cf6 59 times and zero teal; translucent
card surface compiles to #1a24369e across 8 rules.